WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.130
Hank: Good morning, John.

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:02.130
John: Good morning, Hank.

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.970
Where are- oh it's Fort Awesome!

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.900
We must be at the dftba.com warehouse.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:07.960
Whoa.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.770
Oh where's the camera going?

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:11.770
Hank: Goodbye, camera.

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:14.179
John: It's question Tuesday, the day that
it's- it's- it's- it's- it's question Tuesday,

00:00:14.179 --> 00:00:16.521
the day that we answer- it's question Tuesday,
the day that we answer real questions-

00:00:16.521 --> 00:00:17.660
Hank: I'm gonna leave all of those in, just
by the way.

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:18.880
John: I know you will, I know you will.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.039
It's question Tuesday, the day that we answer
real questions from real nerdfighters.

00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:22.039
Hank: It's Friday!

00:00:22.039 --> 00:00:23.439
John: Are you sure that you don't want to
upload this on my day?

00:00:23.439 --> 00:00:24.439
Hank: I'm sure.

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:25.439
John: Alright.

00:00:25.439 --> 00:00:27.489
Hank : I've just asked on Twitter if people
have any questions for us, John.

00:00:27.489 --> 00:00:29.429
Would you like to answer some questions for
people?

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.990
John: Yes, that's how question Tuesday and
Friday work.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:35.130
Hank: Jessica would like to know, "What were
your first cars?"

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.160
John: My first car was a 1991 Volvo 240 named
Arlo.

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:40.160
Hank: Funny!

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.190
That was my first car, too.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.190
[John laughs]

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:46.930
Hank: Actually, uh, after Arlo, uh, got the
same car again, but, uh, white...

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:47.930
John: White.

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:48.930
Hank: ...and smelled more like vomit.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:52.170
John: Hank, how, after so long, have you guys
not gotten tired of each other?

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:53.810
Hank: Oh, I'm so tired of you.

00:00:53.810 --> 00:00:58.430
John: My question is, how, after all this
time, have you guys not gotten tired of us.

00:00:58.430 --> 00:00:59.430
[Hank laughs]

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:00.430
Hank: Hey, John.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:01.430
John: Yes?

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:02.650
Hank: Evelyn would like to know, "How do you
find a nerdfighter at your university?

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:06.689
John: One of my favorite ways is to wear some
kind of, uh, nerdfighter clothing because

00:01:06.689 --> 00:01:08.109
that tends to attract them.

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:10.109
Lots of colleges now have nerdfighter clubs.

00:01:10.109 --> 00:01:14.390
Hank: And if you don't have a nerdfighter
club at your university, you should start

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:15.390
one.

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:16.390
John: You can start one.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.170
Michaela asks, "Who is playing Margo in the
Paper Towns movie?"

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:19.170
Hank?

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:20.170
Hank: Uh, I am.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:21.170
John: Yes!

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:22.869
We have been begging Hank.

00:01:22.869 --> 00:01:24.560
There is no other Margo Roth Spiegelman.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:25.649
That's what we've been saying.

00:01:25.649 --> 00:01:27.280
It's not a passion project for Hank.

00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:28.280
It's just...

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:29.950
Hank: I'm really not interested in the project
itself.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:30.950
John: ...purely financial.

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:33.429
Hank: I'm the Nick Cage of John Green movies.

00:01:33.429 --> 00:01:35.840
I'll do any John Green movie as long as you
pay me enough.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:36.840
[John laughs]

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:37.840
John: Poor Nick Cage.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:38.840
Oh, God.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:39.840
Hank: Hopefully, he doesn't watch.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:40.840
John: He's-

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:42.159
Hank: I am a huge Nick Cage fan, actually.

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:43.539
"This wood is fake."

00:01:43.539 --> 00:01:44.709
John: That Christopher Walken?

00:01:44.709 --> 00:01:46.549
Hank: No, that was Nick Cage from Moonstruck.

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:47.549
John: Is that Jack- Jack Nicholson?

00:01:47.549 --> 00:01:49.939
Hank: How about you sing the answer to the
next question?

00:01:49.939 --> 00:01:50.939
[John grunts.]

00:01:50.939 --> 00:01:51.939
John: Yes.

00:01:51.939 --> 00:01:52.939
Hank: Hey, John.

00:01:52.939 --> 00:01:53.939
John: Yes?

00:01:53.939 --> 00:01:55.729
Hank: Beth would like to know, will she be
able to buy one of those posters you signed?

00:01:55.729 --> 00:01:56.729
John: Yeeessss.

00:01:56.729 --> 00:01:57.729
Is that how you sing?

00:01:57.729 --> 00:02:01.529
Hank: We are at the warehouse right now because
John's been signing posters all day and I've

00:02:01.529 --> 00:02:02.529
just been watching him.

00:02:02.529 --> 00:02:04.659
John: By the way, dftba.com, link in the dooblydoo.

00:02:04.659 --> 00:02:08.190
Or just go to dftba.com, you can just type
it, just five letters.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:12.120
John: Hannah asks "Any advice on strengthening
relationships between siblings?"

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.800
Hank: Make a video blog together.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:19.230
John: I am a big believer, actually, in shared
projects, like Hank and I are a lot closer

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:20.590
because we do stuff together.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.000
Hank: I think that goes for most relationships.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:24.471
John: Henry and I were just making Legos and
it's so fun!

00:02:24.471 --> 00:02:25.530
Hank: Yeah, like yeah.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:26.530
Father son-

00:02:26.530 --> 00:02:27.790
John: He wasn't really doing anything.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.250
Hank: Right, you made Legos and he-

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.600
John: And he was like "Go, dad.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.420
Do it" And then he would be like "That's the
bad guy."

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.590
And I'd be like "I don't know.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:37.860
I mean aren't villains complicated?

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.500
Isn't it - you know we don't know that person's
backstory; we need to learn to imagine them

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:45.210
complexly", and Henry would say "He's REALLY
bad."

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.210
[Hank laughs]

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:47.210
Hank: I have a question.

00:02:47.210 --> 00:02:48.210
John: Yeah.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.210
Hank: Tell me some more stuff Henry says.

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:50.210
[John laughs]

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:52.820
John: I will tell you one more thing; we're
emphasizing learning, how like knowledge is

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:56.270
power, Henry said to Sarah the other day "You
know what's a good kind of learning?"

00:02:56.270 --> 00:03:00.260
and Sarah said "What?" and Henry said "Learning
how to turn on the TV."

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:01.500
[John laughs]

00:03:01.500 --> 00:03:03.350
Hank: How does Henry feel about me?

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:04.350
Is he a fan of Hank?

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:08.150
John: Yeah, no, he said right before I left
to come about here, he said "I would like

00:03:08.150 --> 00:03:11.170
you to give a message to Uncle Hank and Auntie
Katherine, okaboasdsanfdeanrokloghahhh.".

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.590
[John and Hank laugh]

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:16.290
Hank: I'm glad - well I'm glad that that message
got passed on.

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:19.790
John: It was literally the last thing he said
to me before I left, so and I was waiting,

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:25.170
you know I was waiting like I love them, I
miss them, I can't wait to see them, okasafdseslknrtksdfn.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:28.630
Hank: He probably watched my videos and he
knows that that's how I talk.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:29.630
[John laughs]

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:30.630
Hank: John.

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:31.630
John: Yes.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:32.630
Hank: Thank you for doing question Tuesday
with me.

00:03:32.630 --> 00:03:33.630
John: It has been my pleasure.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:34.630
Hank: I'll see you on Tuesday but also...

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:35.630
John and Hank: ...now.

00:03:35.630 --> 00:03:36.630
Hank: It was good.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:39.430
John: The world may be broken, but hope is
not crazy.

00:03:39.430 --> 00:03:41.060
I love unironic enthusiasm.

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:43.830
Hank: How do you express your unironic enthusiasm?

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:47.050
John: Gigigigigigigigigigigigigi generally.

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:48.190
Some version of that.

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:49.190
Sometimes it's internal.

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:50.610
Hank: Can I try?

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:51.610
John: Yeah.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:52.610
Hank: Gigigigigigigigigigigigigi!

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:54.490
John: That's much better than your Nicholas
Cage impression.

00:03:54.490 --> 00:03:56.010
Now you have to put it in the video!

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:56.579
[Hank Laughs]

